ggml: SITU as one GLU op, with CPU and SYCL kernels

HomeBrain patch on ggml, ggml-cpu, ggml-sycl and llama-graph. Applies on top of 0005.
Upstream tracking: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/32757

Inkling 2's MoE activation, beta*tanh(g/beta)*sigmoid(g) * lb*tanh(u/lb), was
nine ops per layer pass (SCALE, TANH, SCALE, SIGMOID, MUL, SCALE, TANH, SCALE,
MUL). GGML_GLU_OP_SITU computes it in one, with beta and linear_beta as params.
build_moe_ffn emits it where the layer's device supports it and keeps the op
chain otherwise, so other backends are unchanged. The CPU kernel follows the
chain's op order (bit-identical to it in f32); the SYCL kernel takes f32 and
f16, like the other GLU kernels.

